        "problem": "Express $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x-{270}^{\u2218})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x$ or $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x-{270}^{\u2218})=$\n{{field-1}}",
        "worked_solution": "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061u\\operatorname{cos}\u2061v-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061u\\operatorname{sin}\u2061v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={270}^{\u2218},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x-{270}^{\u2218}) & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{270}^{\u2218}-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{270}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\cdot (0)-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
